  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Opt 301.07 Prohibition on Pharmaceutical Agents. No optometrist licensed in New Hampshire shall utilize any pharmaceutical agents unless the therapeutic pharmaceutical agent (TPA) or therapeutic pharmaceutical agent/glaucoma (TPA/G) certification has been issued by the OPLC.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Opt 100) #5839, eff 6-17-94, EXPIRED: 6-17-00\n\nNew. #7370, INTERIM, eff 9-30-00, EXPIRED: 3-29-01\n\nNew. #7670, eff 4-4-02; ss by #7889, eff 5-20-03, EXPIRED: 5-20-11\n\nNew. #10243, eff 12-18-12; ss by #12383, eff 9-16-17 (from Opt 301.09); ss by #14242, eff 6-21-25, EXPIRES: 6-21-35 (formerly Opt 301.08)",
